  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Disprove the following statement:\n\nFor any $a,b\\in Z,$ if $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2),$ then $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).$\n\nTo {{field-1}} a universal statement, it's sufficient to find {{field-2}}. \nIn other words, we need to show that {{field-3}}\n\n$$\n{{field-4}}\\,\\text{and}\\,{{field-5}}.\n$$",
